{"eid":"f424038fbe926599","ts":"2026-10-08T03:37:44.674226+00:00","author":"Marek Kobylinski","op":"create","actor_type":"agent","surface":"mcp","session":"eb7f7072-d633-41c2-99f0-ac7420aa010e","agent":"Ivan","detail":{"assignees":[],"attributes":{},"description":"## Outcome\n\nA test reads caught messages over a stable JSON API, waits for one without sleeping, empties the store in its setup, and Sundew delivers provider-shaped status and inbound webhooks to the application.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn — you own `internal/api` and `internal/callback`:\n- `GET /api/v1/messages` — filters `to`, `from`, `body` (contains), `account`, `since` (RFC 3339), `provider`; `limit`, `cursor`. Response `{\"items\":[…],\"next_cursor\":\"…\"}`; items are `core.Message` as JSON.\n- `GET /api/v1/messages/latest` — same filters; the newest match, or 404.\n- `GET /api/v1/messages/{id}`; `DELETE /api/v1/messages/{id}`; `DELETE /api/v1/messages` (all).\n- `GET /api/v1/messages/stream` — Server-Sent Events; each `core.Event` as one event (`event:` its type, `data:` its JSON); the same filters narrow it; a comment line as heartbeat every 15 s; ends cleanly when the client goes.\n- `POST /api/v1/reset` — empties the store, 204.\n- `POST /api/v1/inbound` — JSON `{\"provider\",\"from\",\"to\",\"body\",\"account\",\"media_urls\",\"url\"}`; `provider` defaults to `twilio`; `url` defaults to `Config.InboundURL`, and neither present is a 400. Builds the request through `Providers[provider].InboundRequest`, sends it, stores the message (`Direction: inbound`, `Status: received`), returns the message together with the application's response status.\n- `GET /api/v1/openapi.json` — OpenAPI 3.1 for everything above, generated from or checked against the handlers by a test, so it cannot drift.\n- Errors: one JSON shape, `{\"error\":{\"code\":\"…\",\"message\":\"…\"}}`, with 400 / 404 / 405 / 500.\n- `internal/callback`: subscribes to the bus; for a created outbound message whose `Options[\"status_callback\"]` is set, delivers `queued`, then after `Config.CallbackDelay` `sent`, then after the same delay `delivered` — or `failed` with an error code when `Config.CallbackOutcome` is `failed` — calling `Store.UpdateStatus` before each send and building each request with `Providers[m.Provider].StatusRequest`. A webhook that fails or times out (5 s) is logged and does not stop the sequence. `Reset` or deleting the message cancels what is pending for it. Stops with its context.\n- `scripts/acceptance/30-api.sh` (latest, list, stream delivering a message to a client that connected before it was sent, reset) and `scripts/acceptance/40-callbacks.sh` (a small receiver container records the webhooks: `queued`, `sent`, `delivered` in order with the configured delay; the `failed` outcome; the inbound webhook).\n- README: an \"API for tests\" section.\n\nOut: provider payload shapes (the provider module builds them), the store, the UI, client helper libraries. Do not change `internal/core`; a change you need is a `decide`.\n\n## How to verify\n\nOn this machine, in the lane:\n- `go vet ./...` exits 0; `go test -race ./...` exits 0. Tests use `httptest`, a fake `core.Store`, a fake `core.Bus` and a fake `core.Provider` in the test files; the callback tests use an injected clock or a delay of milliseconds, never a sleep on wall time longer than that.\n- Tests cover: every filter and their combination; paging; latest found / not found; get / delete found / not found; delete all; reset; the stream receiving created, updated, deleted and reset events, a filter narrowing it, and the handler returning when the client disconnects; inbound with `url`, with the configured default, with neither, with an unknown provider; the status sequence for both outcomes, no callback URL, a failing receiver, cancellation by delete and by reset; the OpenAPI document listing every route.\n- After the Foundation and Twilio lanes have merged and you have rebased: your registration lines are in `cmd/sundew/main.go`, and `scripts/acceptance.sh` exits 0 with your steps in it.\n\n## Route\n\n`design`: no. `review_code`: yes. `review_tests`: yes. e2e acceptance: yes — `30-api.sh`, `40-callbacks.sh`; the Reviewer extends them.\n\n## Decided and open\n\n- Start now, against `internal/core` and fakes. You need the Foundation lane merged to run for real, and the Twilio lane merged for `40-callbacks.sh`; you raise `build` after both. Conflicts in `go.mod`, `go.sum`, `docs/dependencies.md` and the registration block are yours to resolve on rebase.\n- Stream is SSE, not long-poll (the brief allows either; SSE serves both tests and the UI).\n- `SUNDEW_INBOUND_URL` is the \"configured application webhook\" of the brief's acceptance item 6; a `url` in the request overrides it.\n- `Since` and `since` compare against `created_at`.\n- The error code for a failed outcome is the provider module's to choose; the engine passes `\"30008\"` for Twilio only if the provider leaves it empty — ask the Twilio lane's Programmer on that task which it returns.\n- Package layout, ownership and proof rules: `docs/architecture.md`. Go here, Docker possibly remote, containers only: `docs/journal/2026-10-08/decision-go-runs-locally-remote-host-runs-only-containers.md`.\n\n## Where to look\n\n`internal/core/core.go`, `docs/architecture.md`, the brief (`docs/journal/2026-10-08/draft-sundew-brief.md`: \"What it is\" items 4–6, acceptance items 4, 5, 6, 8).","labels":[],"priority":"high","status":"open","title":"Query API, stream, reset, callback engine and inbound simulator"}}
